# taken from NIST Circuit Complexity:
# https://github.com/usnistgov/Circuits/blob/master/data/slp/aes/aes-sbox-fwd-g113-a32-d27-ad6.slp
# NIST project listing:
# https://github.com/usnistgov/Circuits/blob/master/data/slp/aes/README.md
# paper cited by NIST (Boyar, Matthews, Peralta):
# https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-012-9124-7
#
# NIST notes that this circuit is based on that work and was subsequently
# improved by two XOR gates. It was not one of the seven S-box rows benchmarked
# in Table 4 of CCHPC1.1.
#
# normalized interface: x0..x7 / s0..s7, index 0 = AES byte MSB.
#
# Unrail results:
# NL: total=32, DR=14, DR2SR_B2F=18
# L:  total=81, DR=52, SR_F2B=1, SR_B2F=28
# REG=8
#
# #gates:     113
# depth (NL):  27 (6)
# #L:          81
# #NL:         32
